{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18043 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Arjunglucoside I appears to have a complex network of targets that ultimately lead to HepG2, a human hepatocellular carcinoma cell line. The evidence suggests that Arjunglucoside I acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which is itself targeted by methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, and this pathway culminates in HepG2. Similarly, Arjunglucoside I is also linked to Raji, a cell line that targets Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, which also targets HepG2. Additionally, Arjunglucoside I is associated with Hepatocyte, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which also targets HepG2. These findings collectively suggest that Arjunglucoside I may exert its effects through multiple distinct pathways, ultimately leading to the inhibition of HepG2. The integration of these targets highlights the potential for Arjunglucoside I to act as a multi-target compound, influencing cellular processes in HepG2 through different molecular mechanisms.",
